WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.260
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
For many Cloud users,

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.460
billing is just
something you deal

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:03.810
with at the end of the month.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.857
But for larger teams
and organizations,

00:00:05.857 --> 00:00:07.440
you'll hit a scale
at which it becomes

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.840
critical to understand
costs and to manage

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.220
what you're paying for.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.010
On this episode of
"Beyond Your Bill,"

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.000
we'll go into more depth
on billing accounts,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.760
the payments profile, and
managing billing permissions.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.125
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.530
In the last video, we
looked at an overview of how

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:29.512
GCP resources are organized.

00:00:29.512 --> 00:00:31.220
In order to make sure
those resources are

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:34.490
paid for correctly, the billing
account and payments profile

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.710
need to be set up with
the right permissions.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.320
See, some GCP services
have free tiers.

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.660
But you won't be able
to go beyond that tier

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.985
without having to wait
to pay for all the usage.

00:00:43.985 --> 00:00:46.555
All services need to exist
as part of a project.

00:00:46.555 --> 00:00:48.680
And each project will need
to have a single billing

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.380
account associated with it,
though a billing account can

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.090
have multiple
associated projects.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:54.590
And the billing
reports and invoice

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:57.245
will be able to break
down costs by project.

00:00:57.245 --> 00:00:59.120
Billing accounts will
also be directly linked

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.510
to a Google payments profile,
which sits outside the Cloud

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.519
and is used to pay for
all Google services,

00:01:04.519 --> 00:01:06.680
like G Suite and Google Ads.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.860
If Google Cloud Platform is the
only Google service you use,

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.300
you may not interact much
with the payments profile.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.020
However, it's important to keep
track of both billing accounts

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.790
and payments
profiles, especially

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:20.210
for larger organizations using
multiple products and services.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.950
For GCP, think of
the billing account

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:24.800
as the way to organize all
your Cloud-specific billing,

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.230
and the payments profile for
how to actually pay and view

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.400
invoices.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.340
Both have their own
sets of permissions,

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.090
so you can control who
can view and manage

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.710
the different accounts.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:36.770
We recommend setting up multiple
administrators for each of them

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:40.340
to safeguard against any issues
and to review them regularly.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.625
It could even end up being
the same admins for both.

00:01:42.625 --> 00:01:44.750
It's also a good idea to
only have a single billing

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.730
account and a single
payments profile

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.590
to help make it
easier to manage them.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.050
Having multiple can make cost
management complicated down

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:51.620
the road.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:54.180
So stick to as few as possible.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.510
Let's look at setting up and
managing an online billing

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:59.293
account, which is paid with a
credit card or a bank account.

00:01:59.293 --> 00:02:00.710
As your company
grows, you'll want

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.800
to work with the GCP Sales team
to set up an offline billing

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.657
account, which is
paid with invoices.

00:02:05.657 --> 00:02:08.240
Either way, you need to be able
to manage your billing account

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:10.729
permissions through the GCP
Console and the payments

00:02:10.729 --> 00:02:12.220
profile online.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:14.600
In the console, you can
open up the left navigation

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.980
and choose Billing to see
your current billing accounts.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:18.980
You may need to click on
Manage Billing Accounts

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:20.090
to get to the right page.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.817
And then click on
Create Account.

00:02:21.817 --> 00:02:23.900
Choose a descriptive name
for the billing account,

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.433
and choose a location, which
determines the currency.

00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:28.100
Each billing account
and related invoice

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.522
can only represent
a single currency.

00:02:30.522 --> 00:02:32.480
You'll then need to set
up the payments profile

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.460
and can choose between
individual and business.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.290
This can't be changed later.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.780
You'll also be able to choose
the primary contact, who

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.270
will be the administrator
for the payments profile.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.940
Again, we recommend
setting up multiple admins

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.340
or using a group to ensure a
reasonable level of redundancy.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.590
The payments profile will
need a form of payment,

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:51.500
such as a credit card
or a bank account.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.020
For more redundancy, you
should actually come back later

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:56.610
and add an additional form
of payment as a backup,

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.280
as well as reviewing
your administrators

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.273
and your notification settings.

00:03:00.273 --> 00:03:01.940
Once the new billing
account is created,

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.410
or if you're working with
an existing billing account,

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.910
you'll be able to manage it
from the right side, or the Info

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:07.430
panel.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.140
The best thing to
start with is to add

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.400
an additional administrator.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:13.160
You can do this by clicking
the Add Members button.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.960
You can add individual
users this way,

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.058
or you can add a group.

00:03:16.058 --> 00:03:17.600
So there won't be
any access concerns

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.880
when you need to find the
billing account admin.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.850
In addition, you can also add
billing account viewers, who

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:24.728
have view-only
access to information

00:03:24.728 --> 00:03:27.020
like how much each project
associated with this billing

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.140
account costs, as well as
billing account users, who

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.990
can not only view the details,
but also associate projects

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.393
with this billing account.

00:03:34.393 --> 00:03:35.810
Once you've set
up your users, you

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.855
can then create new projects,
or take existing projects

00:03:38.855 --> 00:03:40.730
and associate them with
this billing account.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.230
Similar to billing
accounts, you can

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.360
manage permissions for
projects and folders

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.520
by adding users and
assigning roles.

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.455
You can even create
your own custom roles

00:03:48.455 --> 00:03:50.330
and choose the exact
breakdown of permissions

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.770
that a user can have.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:54.080
Giving a user view
access to a project

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.870
will let them see costs only
for that project, as opposed

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.060
to a billing account
viewer, who can see costs

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:01.603
for all projects associated
with that billing account.

00:04:01.603 --> 00:04:03.770
If you need to change
information about the payments

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:07.190
profile, you'll do that
from payments.google.com,

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.170
rather than the GCP console.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.880
As I've mentioned,
it's critical to make

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:13.610
sure to review the users and
permissions on both billing

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.250
accounts and payments
profile regularly, perhaps

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.920
every quarter, and to make
sure that your team knows

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.323
who the administrators are.

00:04:20.323 --> 00:04:21.740
In case of any
issues, you'll want

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:23.990
to contact the billing
account administrators

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:26.750
and have them reach out to
Billing Support as needed.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.490
With that set up,
you can now make sure

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.770
any GCP services are
paid for correctly,

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.590
and that your organization
is set up to manage costs.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.620
Check out the links for a deeper
dive and more best practices

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:39.440
around managing your billing
account and payments profile.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.940
In the next video,
we'll look at how

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.340
to directly examine
your costs using billing

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.990
reports in the GCP console.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.340
[MUSIC PLAYING]

